{
  "requirement": "The bundled skills MUST direct agents to make a requirement distributed only when its obligation applies on its own at each of many sites, such as a convention every validation function follows; to use `{impl}` instead when particular code carries out the requirement as a whole; and to mark with `{impl}` the code that carries out any obligation of a distributed requirement that its sites do not uphold.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has three obligations. The bundled skills must direct agents to (1) make a requirement distributed only when its obligation applies on its own at each site, (2) use `{impl}` when particular code carries out the requirement as a whole, and (3) mark with `{impl}` the code that carries out any obligation its sites do not uphold.\n\nThe requirement's own `:impl:` anchor names `assets/skills/habeas/references/distributed-requirements.md`, so that file carries the guidance. Its `## Do` section contains the paragraph \"Make a requirement distributed only when its obligation applies on its own at each site; when particular code carries out the requirement as a whole, use `{impl}` there.\" I found no other skill that carries this guidance.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_make_a_requirement_distributed_only_for_per_site_obligations]` is marked `{test}`. It reads the `## Do` section of that reference through `distributed_reference()` and `section()`. It then asserts with `assert_text` that the section contains these two sentences:\n- \"Make a requirement distributed only when its obligation applies on its own at each site; when particular code carries out the requirement as a whole, use `{impl}` there.\"\n- \"Separate obligations each site upholds from obligations particular code carries out, and mark that code `{impl}`.\"\n\n`assert_text` panics if either phrase is missing. The first assertion covers obligations (1) and (2). The second covers obligation (3), because the guidance is to separate site-upheld obligations from code-carried ones and mark that code `{impl}`. The test would fail if the guidance were removed or reversed.\n\nThe test does not check the illustrative \"many sites\" or \"every validation function\" wording. Those are an example in the requirement, not separate obligations. It also checks only the one reference file, but that file is the designated implementation, so I don't count that as a gap.",
  "references": "78662a5f93bdc1cce2c30f2a56821845f344b48e61610e0248463e30f52ffe47",
